# Idempotency and retry semantics

The agent (or the auto-design loop, Phase 7) WILL retry calls. Pipe disconnects, AutoCAD hangs, etc. Tools must behave predictably under retry.

## Tool flavors

| Flavor      | Property        | Examples                                | Retry semantics                                        |
| ----------- | --------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Read        | `ReadOnly=true` | `list_layers`, `get_entity_handle`      | Always safe to retry; cache by args+document handle    |
| Idempotent  | n/a             | `set_layer_color`, `apply_layer_standard` | Retrying produces same final state; record `idempotencyKey` in result |
| Creator     | n/a             | `draw_circle`, `create_block`           | NOT idempotent by default; use `dedupKey` arg for opt-in |
| Mutator     | n/a             | `move_entities`, `rotate_entities`      | NOT idempotent (move twice = double); rely on checkpoints |

## Rules

1. **Read-only tools** must NOT call `LockDocument` and must NOT start a write transaction.
2. **Idempotent tools** must verify-before-write. E.g., `set_layer_color` first reads current color; if same, returns early with `noop: true`.
3. **Creator tools** that the user wants idempotent must accept `dedupKey: string?`. If a previous call with same key created an entity AND it still exists, return that handle instead.
4. **Mutator tools** rely on the agent using `acad_undo_checkpoint` / `acad_restore_checkpoint` (Phase 7). Document this in `description`.
5. **Long operations** (e.g., `validate_drawing`) MUST honor `CancellationToken` and check it inside loops at most every 100 ms.

## Example: idempotent layer color

```csharp
[McpTool(name: "set_layer_color", description: "Set RGB color of a layer. Idempotent: noop if already that color.",
         category: "layers", Intent = new[] { ... })]
public static SetLayerColorResult SetLayerColor(SetLayerColorArgs args, CancellationToken ct)
{
    var current = LayerHelpers.GetColor(args.LayerName);
    if (current.Equals(args.Color))
    {
        return new SetLayerColorResult(args.LayerName, args.Color, Noop: true);
    }
    LayerHelpers.SetColor(args.LayerName, args.Color);
    return new SetLayerColorResult(args.LayerName, args.Color, Noop: false);
}
```

## Example: dedupKey on creator

```csharp
[McpTool(name: "create_layer", description: "Create a layer. Pass dedupKey to make idempotent.",
         category: "layers", Intent = new[] { ... })]
public static CreateLayerResult CreateLayer(CreateLayerArgs args, CancellationToken ct)
{
    if (LayerHelpers.Exists(args.Name)) {
        return new CreateLayerResult(args.Name, Created: false);
    }
    LayerHelpers.Create(args.Name, args.Color);
    return new CreateLayerResult(args.Name, Created: true);
}
```
